{"id":1411,"date":"2020-11-27T16:14:21","date_gmt":"2020-11-28T00:14:21","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1411"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:40:33","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:40:33","slug":"install-arduino-and-rokit-files-macos","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/install-arduino-and-rokit-files-macos\/","title":{"rendered":"Device Setup"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215e47b7d8\" name=\"6a2215e47b7d8\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Download and install Arduino<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]If you want to run your own code on your Rokit Smart bots, you&#8217;ll need Arduino. Luckily you can download Arduino IDE directly from the\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.arduino.cc\/en\/Main\/Software\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-link-type=\"LINK\">website<\/a>\u00a0for free!<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Find the version that matches your operating system.<\/li>\n<li>Download and install that version of Arduino.<\/li>\n<li>Run the Arduino IDE by double-clicking on the Arduino icon.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>* If you need a visual, we have a video for you!<\/p>\n<p>* Make sure you install the latest version of Arduino. If you are using a Mac device, try to have the latest OS to make sure it is compatible with Arduino.<\/p>\n<p>* Do not use the app store or web editor versions of Arduino. Please use the website link provided.[\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=RKZzQajAid4&#8243; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215e47b8fe\" name=\"6a2215e47b8fe\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Install RokitSmart library<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Open Arduino and go to Sketch &gt; Include Library &gt; Manage Libraries&#8230; in the menu.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;3002&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Search for &#8220;RokitSmart&#8221; and install the library. Always install the latest version![\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7243&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215e47b96d\" name=\"6a2215e47b96d\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Install board files<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]On Mac, open Arduino &gt; Preferences.<\/p>\n<p>On Windows, open File &gt; Settings.<\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;3005&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]This will open the Preferences window.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;3006&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Look for a text box labeled &#8220;Additional Boards Manager URLs&#8221;.<\/p>\n<p>Copy and paste this link in that textbox: https:\/\/raw.githubusercontent.com\/RobolinkInc\/Robolink\/master\/package_rokit_index.json<\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;3007&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Now that you have added the URL, you can close the window and open the Board Manager.<\/p>\n<p>Do this by going to Tools &gt; Board: &gt; Boards Manager&#8230; in the menu.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;3008&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Search for &#8220;rokit&#8221; and install the board files. Make sure you install the latest version![\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7242&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215e47ba31\" name=\"6a2215e47ba31\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Driver installation<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Click <a href=\"https:\/\/www.silabs.com\/products\/development-tools\/software\/interface#cp210x\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-link-type=\"LINK\">here<\/a>\u00a0to download the CP210x driver for your operating system.<\/li>\n<li>Unzip the downloaded file then open or run the VCP Installation Driver.<\/li>\n<li>After installation, open the \u201cDevice Manager\u201d and click on the Ports (COM&amp; LPT) tab. Pay attention to the COM port number! It should match the COM port that is listed in the\u00a0Arduino IDE\u2019s Port tab, which is under Tools &gt; Ports.<\/li>\n<li>See the video below for a walkthrough with Windows<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=fBIUXdI-bvo&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<strong>Attention Mac Users:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Make sure you are on the latest OS if possible (Catalina is incompatible)<\/li>\n<li>If you are having trouble uploading code later, try reinstalling the driver a second time.<\/li>\n<li>If you are still having trouble, install the version inside of the &#8220;Legacy&#8221; folder.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1821&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;920&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 5 Download and install Arduino [vc_column_text]If you want to run your own code on your Rokit Smart bots, you'll need Arduino. Luckily you can download Arduino IDE directly&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/install-arduino-and-rokit-files-macos\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1734,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":802,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1753,1777,1793],"lesson-tag":[2163,2184,2218,2177,2170,2222,2122,2172,2171],"class_list":["post-1411","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-arduino-ide","lesson-tag-computer-science","lesson-tag-getting-started","lesson-tag-installation","lesson-tag-macos","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-robotics","lesson-tag-rokit-smart","module-getting-started","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1411","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":7,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1411\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":7244,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1411\/revisions\/7244"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1734"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1411"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=1411"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=1411"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https: